note bottom of R #E3F2FD
  **One false positive, recorded so it is not re-raised.** The backend's
  "".unwrap_or_default()"" on list reads has F1's exact shape — a failure
  becoming an empty success — and is correct: ""get_data_or_none"" maps only
  ""ReturnValueMissing"" to ""None"" and propagates every real error, so an
  empty list can never stand in for a failed read.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<#FFEBEE>| high severity |
  |<#FFF3E0>| medium severity |
  |<#FFFDE7>| low severity |
  |<#E8F5E9>| searched, nothing found |
  |<#E3F2FD>| the search itself |
  |<#ECEFF1>| the pattern it came from |
endlegend
